  "intro_html": "<p>This gentle stroll goes from the summit station of the funicular – with almost 90 per cent maximum inclination it is one of the steepest in the world – on a tarred small road to the dam of Lago Ritom and subsequently along the north shore of the lake to Cadagno di Fuori. From there you hike on a dirt road past Alpe Piora to Capanna Cadagno. Especially on a clear summer week-end there is traffic on the road to the artificial lake (thus for the first 20 minutes). Between the dam and Cadagno di Fuori, however, it should be quieter: uphill the road is closed between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m., downhill between 9 a.m. and noon. The segment is also popular among mountain bikers.</p>\n<p>If you depart from the dam (car parking), you save about 20 minutes.</p>",
